<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11602" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπᾰτάω</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰπ</span>], late 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπασχολ-έω</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Luc.
			<u>Syr.D.</u>
			27
		</span></i> (
			Pass.
		): impf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠπάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					938
				</span></i>
			, 
				Ion.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ-απάτασκον</span> Orac. in <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				1070
			</span></i>: fut.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ήσω</span>: aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠπάτησα,</span>
			
				Ion.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπ-</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.344
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				500
			</span></i> (lyr.): pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠπάτηκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					929
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, fut.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπατηθήσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>APr.</u>
					67a38
				</span></i>
			, cf. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ-</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Cra.</u>
				436b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				2.123
			</span></i>; also in 
				Med.
			 form 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπατήσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					262a
				</span></i>
			, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ-</span>) <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				7.3.3
			</span></i>: aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠπατήθην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Cri.</u>
					52e
				</span></i>
			: pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠπάτημαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					5.46
				</span></i>
			, etc.: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπάτη</span>):—<i>cheat, deceive,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				19.97
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				17.139
			</span></i>, etc.; <i>cheat</i> one's <i>hopes,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				462
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἷ᾽ ἠπάτηκας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					929
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλέμματα . . ἂ τὸν πολέμιον ἀπατήσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					5.9
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i>to be deceptive</i> or <i>fallacious,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1376b28
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be self-deceived, mistaken,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				182
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				594
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				262a
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔγνωκα . . φωτὸς ἠπατημένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					807
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί γὰρ οὐκ . . ἔρχεται ἀγγελίας
				ἀπατώμενον;</span> comes not <i>belied by</i> the result?
				<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>El.</u>
				170
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. περί τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1368b22
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περί τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Sens.</u>
					442b8
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ταύτην τὴν ἀπάτην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>AP</u>
					0.74a6
				</span></i>
			; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπατᾶσθαι ὡς . .</span>
			<i>to be deceived into thinking</i> that . ., <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				323a
			</span></i>.—The compd. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξαπατάω</span> is more common, esp. in <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
			</span></i> and 
				Att.
			 Prose; the simple Verb is used in <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ge.</u>
				3.13
			</span></i>, al., but not by <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
			</span></i>, and is rare in later Greek, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.15d
			</span></i>.</div>
